  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "P7spDehDffc0Pkq3jNQ2xGfYsJ4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:45.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The convenience of `IReactorClient` costs you error fidelity. On a `FAILED` job the client rethrows the message and nothing else:\n\n```typescript\n// inside ReactorClient, after the job reaches a terminal status\nif (job.status === JobStatus.FAILED) {\n  throw new Error(job.error?.message);\n}\n```\n\nThe same pattern runs in `execute`, `executeBatch`, `create`, `deleteDocument`, `deleteDocuments`, `addRelationship`, and `removeRelationship`. Two consequences:\n\n- The thrown `Error.message` equals `job.error?.message`, which **can be `undefined`** if `error` was never set. Guard before displaying it.\n- The original error class, stack, and `errorHistory` are gone. You cannot `instanceof` your way to a diagnosis at this boundary.\n\nTo recover the detail, drop to the lower-level `IReactor.getJobStatus(jobId)` and read the `JobInfo`:\n\n```typescript\ntype JobInfo = {\n  id: string; documentId: string; status: JobStatus;\n  error?: { message: string; stack: string };        // the failing error\n  errorHistory?: Array<{ message: string; stack: string }>; // one per attempt, oldest first\n  job?: Job;                                          // populated on failure for debugging\n  consistencyToken: ConsistencyToken; meta: JobMeta;\n  // ...\n};\n```\n\n`errorHistory` is the payoff: a job the queue retried carries **every** failure, with `error` being the most recent. That is invisible from the client boundary, where you see one message. The `{ message, stack }` shape is structural \u2014 treat it as a type you match, not one you import; the barrel's exported `ErrorInfo` is a different (worker-protocol) type aliased as `WorkerErrorInfo`.\n\nSeveral internal write-path errors lose their typed identity at this edge and survive only as a message string: `DocumentDeletedError`, `DocumentNotFoundError`, `CreateDocumentRequiredError`, `InvalidSignatureError`, and `UpgradeManifestNotFoundError`. None are exported, so branching on them means matching `err.message` \u2014 brittle by construction.\n\nRelated edge: `ReactorClient.deleteDocument` throws a plain `new Error(\"Operation aborted\")` rather than an `AbortError` when its signal fires during cascade traversal, so prefer handling that call without relying on `err.name === \"AbortError\"`.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/08-ErrorHandling.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:45.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:45.000Z"
    }
  },
